      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I cannot prioritize students or create intervention lists based on zip codes, socioeconomic status, or racial demographics because such proxies for resource allocation are scientifically proven to introduce harmful bias and violate ethical standards. While environmental factors like neighborhood stressors are significant in real-world sociology, using an AI tool to operationalize them for individual student screening risks automating systemic inequities rather than solving them. A responsible predictive model in this context must explicitly exclude protected characteristics and rely solely on verified, individual-specific behavioral data to ensure fairness and protection for all students.",
